# CLAUDE.md · The Mat (AlgebraMat)

## What this is
A free, static algebra practice site for Karl's middle school students: Vite + plain JavaScript, hosted on GitHub Pages. Three sections of cards (Count it, Build it, Solve it), five problems per level. Progress lives in the browser (localStorage) with a save code, and syncs anonymously to Karl's Google Sheet. Students use school Chromebooks first, phones second. Karl has limited coding knowledge: explain only as much as he needs, briefly.

## Authority order
1. `SPEC-SOLVE-IT-LOOP.md` (the shared Solve it loop, with its conformance checklist)
2. The card spec (`SPEC-<CARD>.md`)
3. Build briefs (`BUILD-BRIEF-*.md`)
4. `DECISION-LOG.md`: history only; some lines were later reversed.

Where code and a spec disagree, report it; don't silently pick one.

## Where things live
- **Specs, briefs, logs:** the repo root (`SPEC-*.md`, `BUILD-BRIEF-*.md`, `DECISION-LOG.md`, `DESIGN-HANDOFF.md`). Audit: `docs/audit/`. Handoff notes: `docs/handoff/NEXT.md`.
- **Entry:** `index.html`, `src/main.js` (routing, saving, sync, keyboard).
- **Cards:** `src/packs/index.js` (each card's levels and generator; `SECTIONS`); `src/play/` (one adapter per card or level type, chosen in `main.js`); `src/engine/` (logic, generators, slips; no DOM); `src/view/` (screens). Styles: `src/style.css`.
- **Save code and progress:** `src/engine/progress.js` (code v14, one bit per level; migrations; legacy credit); `src/storage.js`.
- **Sync:** `src/engine/sync.js`, `src/sync.js`, `src/syncStore.js`, `src/view/account.js`; sheet side `teacher/Code.gs`, `teacher/RosterSync.gs`, `teacher/SETUP.md`.
- **Deploy:** `.github/workflows/ci-deploy.yml`: tests and build on every push; deploys to Pages only from `main`.
- **Tests:** `tests/` (Vitest, `npm test`). Run them, and `npm run build`, before every push.

## Shared-components registry (details: `docs/audit/02-registry.md`)
| Piece | File | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| The Solve it loop | `src/engine/solveLoop.js` `createSolveLoop` | Choice at every state, forced move, substitution, fold, Undo, Start over, help ladder. Divide it uses it; Add to both sides does not yet. |
| Choice prompt | `src/engine/solveLoop.js` `CHOICE_PROMPT`, `CHOICE_BUTTONS` | The one prompt and its two buttons. |
| Substitution renderer | `src/engine/solveTerms.js` `substitutionLines` | Value placed on x, one operation a line, step highlight; the loop's test cases. |
| Solve it screen pieces | `src/view/solveScreen.js` | The line, work-stack rows, answer row, Check / Next, drag onto x, help row, Undo. |
| Move / Why? panel | `src/view/lightScreen.js` `movePanel`, `moveIcon` | The full move list with Why? boxes. |
| Seesaw | `src/view/addBothMat.js` `drawBalance` | The balance with counters, tipping or level. |
| Group diagram | `src/view/groupDiagram.js` | A fraction of a group: n groups, a bracket on the kept one. |
| Shared messages | `src/view/addBothFeedback.js` | The loop's shared lines (choice, greyed moves...). |
| Number pad | `src/view/quiz.js` `buildPad` | The integer pad (most cards still have their own; see R11). |
| Save code | `src/engine/progress.js` | Encode / decode; one bit per level. |
| Anonymous sync | `src/engine/sync.js`, `src/sync.js` | Sends progress and the anonymous log; merges level by level. |

Several shared pieces still live in card files (`addBothMat.js`, `lightScreen.js`, `addBothFeedback.js`). The plan to move them to one shared folder is `docs/audit/06-refactor-plan.md`. When a piece moves, update this table in the same change.

## Hard rules (never break)
- **Scrambled ids only to the class sheet** (district rule). No names, emails or real ids leave the device.
- **Save codes hold one bit per level,** so a card's level count is fixed. Never rename a pack id. A level-count change needs a migration and a new save-code version.
- **Never overwrite more progress with less:** saves and syncs merge level by level; a finished level stays finished.
- **Answers are whole numbers,** typed on the integer pad.
- **Every generated problem is verified by substitution in code.** No hand-typed banks.
- **Printables are low-ink:** outlines, no filled heading boxes, no grid.

## Reuse before you build
Before writing anything for a card, search the registry above and the repo. If you create a reusable piece, add it to the registry in the same change.

## Working agreements

Working agreements: sessions and models
Start of every session: read this file, `docs/design/SPEC-SOLVE-IT-LOOP.md` and its conformance checklist, the card spec and the brief being worked on, and `docs/handoff/NEXT.md` if it exists. Check the registry before writing anything.
Definition of done: the conformance checklist has been run and its results reported; the registry is updated; this file is updated if the structure changed; a handoff note is written.
Tell Karl to start a fresh session. Say so plainly at the end of your reply, and say what to paste, when: a card or brief is finished and reported; the kind of task is changing (audit or refactor, card build, bug fix); you have re-read the same files more than once or your work is drifting from the specs; earlier context is being summarised away; or a new section or card is starting. Don't wait to be asked.
Before ending a session, write `docs/handoff/NEXT.md`: what is done, what is in progress, decisions made, files touched, what to read first, open questions.
Model guidance. Tell Karl when a change of model is worth it. Strongest available (Claude Fable 5.1 or Claude Opus 5.5): audits, refactors that touch shared components, changes to the loop or the architecture, bugs that cross cards, anything where a wrong structural choice is expensive. Mid-tier (Claude Sonnet 5.5): building a card from a finished spec, fixes from a brief. Light (Claude Haiku 5.5): mechanical edits (copy changes, renames, formatting) and re-running checklists. When unsure, say which tier you would choose and why. Keep this list current as models change.
Reuse before you build. If something you are about to build might already exist, stop and search the registry and the repo first.
